{
  "$schema": "https://kinetixui.com/schema/icon-mapping.json",
  "description": "Cross-platform mapping for icons KinetixUI COMPONENTS render internally (their own expand chevron, checkmark, close button, etc.) — not icons a caller passes in as a prop/children/slot, which stay free-form per platform by design. lucide-react is the React source; each native port uses its platform's own icon mechanism: Material Icons on Flutter, SF Symbols on SwiftUI, and on Jetpack Compose Material icons drawn from the module's internal KinetixIcons vectors (material3 Icon, no material-icons dependency). Until the 2026-10-05 icon audit (docs/audits/ICON-ARCHITECTURE-AUDIT.md) every Compose component-owned icon was a Unicode glyph in a Text; the ones that remain are listed, with their reason, in composeGlyphs below, and `pnpm check:icons` fails on any glyph not listed there. `rtl` is the direction rule per icon: 'mirrors' icons must use each platform's direction-aware variant (checked), 'fixed' ones must not turn around. This file only covers icon names reused across two or more components; /docs/icons is the user-facing guide.",
  "types": {
    "icon-ref": "a named icon reference: Flutter Icons.*, a SwiftUI SF Symbol systemName, or a Compose KinetixIcons.* vector (Material icon path data, internal to the module)",
    "glyph": "a literal Unicode character rendered as plain text (e.g. Compose's Text(text = \"✓\")), not a named icon asset. TalkBack reads it aloud and its shape depends on the device font, so each remaining one is recorded in composeGlyphs with its reason.",
    "shape": "a custom-drawn shape (Circle(), CircleShape, BoxShape.circle, Canvas), not an icon or a text glyph",
    "absent": "no hardcoded icon-like element found in this platform's port of this component — verified by grep, not assumed. Usually means the platform's own built-in widget draws its own affordance (e.g. a native context-menu's checkmark), or the element genuinely isn't rendered on that platform."
  },
